Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will be used  
(id is the PK of each table unless stated otherwise)

posts_answers  
• `owner_user_id` : filter answers that belong to user 1908967  
• `creation_date` : keep only answers before 2018‑06‑07  
• `id` : join key to `votes.post_id` (to count votes cast on the answer)  
• `parent_id` : join key to the corresponding question in `posts_questions`

posts_questions  
• `id` : join key from `posts_answers.parent_id`  
• `tags` : list of tags (format “<tag1><tag2>…>”) that will be split and scored

votes  
• `post_id` : the answer that received the vote  
• `vote_type_id` : 2 = up‑vote (worth 10 pts), 1 = accepted‑answer vote (worth 15 pts)  
• `creation_date` (optional) – not needed because we only care about votes on answers filtered by creation date

Typical conditions  
• `owner_user_id = 1908967`  
• `creation_date < '2018-06-07'`  
• `vote_type_id IN (1,2)`  
• use `REGEXP_EXTRACT_ALL(tags,r'<([^>]+)>')` to explode the tag string


